assistant: Subject: Accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Starting with vendor API version 2026-10-01, `created_at` comes back as a number of milliseconds since 1970 (for example `1792142857943`) instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` turned the value into a string and ran `Date.parse` on it. That returned `NaN`, the `|| 0` fallback turned it into 0, and the tool reported every order as placed on 1970-01-01. The fix in `src/tools/get_order.ts` passes a number straight to `new Date` and keeps the old string path for v1, so v1 output doesn't change. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test.

Subject: Accept epoch-millisecond created_at in get_order

Starting with vendor API version 2026-10-01, `created_at` comes back as a number of milliseconds since 1970 (for example `1792142857943`) instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` turned the value into a string and ran `Date.parse` on it. That returned `NaN`, the `|| 0` fallback turned it into 0, and the tool reported every order as placed on 1970-01-01. The fix in `src/tools/get_order.ts` passes a number straight to `new Date` and keeps the old string path for v1, so v1 output doesn't change. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test.
